@TroySchmidt I'd say honestly: that's getting to "a different library" territory since it's not our goal to generate complex SQL in Dapper. It's both _very_ complicated to maintain (across DB providers), but also hard to make generic (e.g. arrays in Postgres vs. IN list in SQL vs. string split in newer SQL, etc.). It's also crazy complex when you get into nested children, applies, etc. Abstracting this away a great deal then gets both hard to implement and confusing to use past the simplest case.

Overall, it sounds like something that'd be more aimed at the https://github.com/henkmollema/Dapper-FluentMap style - would suggest proposing an issue there and seeing if they're interested in such? Otherwise: you're getting into Entity Framework territory.

